<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xml:lang="en"><generator uri="https://jekyllrb.com/" version="4.4.1">Jekyll</generator><link href="https://romain-thomas-shef.github.io/rt/feed.xml" rel="self" type="application/atom+xml"/><link href="https://romain-thomas-shef.github.io/rt/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="en"/><updated>2026-08-31T11:59:15+00:00</updated><id>https://romain-thomas-shef.github.io/rt/feed.xml</id><title type="html">blank</title><subtitle>A simple, whitespace theme for academics. Based on [*folio](https://github.com/bogoli/-folio) design. </subtitle><entry><title type="html">Saintelyon 2025</title><link href="https://romain-thomas-shef.github.io/rt/blog/2025/saintelyon/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Saintelyon 2025"/><published>2025-11-30T12:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2025-11-30T12:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://romain-thomas-shef.github.io/rt/blog/2025/saintelyon</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://romain-thomas-shef.github.io/rt/blog/2025/saintelyon/"><![CDATA[<p>Here we are! Last race of the year, and by far my favorite! What not to like, in my hometown (Saint-Etienne, France; so a good chance to see the family!) and a start in the middle of the night! This is a winter race so the weather is always a bit of a lottery. I was a bit anxious about this year as the last one killed my feet. I had chosen the wronf pair of shoes and it really hurt me. But this year it went well! The weather was ok, not too cold, no rain, a bit of fog and humidity. However, it has rained quite a lot in the days/weeks leading to the race so the trail was basically made of rivers of mud. It was fun! I finished the 80k and 2.2k of climb in 10:43, including pit stops. Ranking was 2661/6609, my best ranking on the race.</p> <swiper-container style="height: 500px;" keyboard="true" navigation="true" pagination="true" pagination-clickable="true" pagination-dynamic-bullets="true" rewind="true"> <swiper-slide style="display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; height: 100%;"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025saintelyon/STL4-480.webp 480w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025saintelyon/STL4-800.webp 800w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025saintelyon/STL4-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025saintelyon/STL4.png" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 m-0" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide style="display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center;"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025saintelyon/STL1-480.webp 480w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025saintelyon/STL1-800.webp 800w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025saintelyon/STL1-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025saintelyon/STL1.png" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 m-0" width="300px" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide style="display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; height: 100%;"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025saintelyon/STL2-480.webp 480w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025saintelyon/STL2-800.webp 800w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025saintelyon/STL2-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025saintelyon/STL2.png" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 m-0" width="300px" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide style="display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; height: 100%;"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025saintelyon/STL3-480.webp 480w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025saintelyon/STL3-800.webp 800w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025saintelyon/STL3-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025saintelyon/STL3.png" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 m-0" width="300px" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide style="display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; height: 100%;"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025saintelyon/STL5-480.webp 480w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025saintelyon/STL5-800.webp 800w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025saintelyon/STL5-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025saintelyon/STL5.png" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 m-0" width="300px" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide style="display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; height: 100%;"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025saintelyon/STL6-480.webp 480w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025saintelyon/STL6-800.webp 800w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025saintelyon/STL6-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025saintelyon/STL6.png" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 m-0" width="300px" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> </swiper-container>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="ultra"/><category term="50miles"/><category term="objective"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Last ultra of the year]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Morunner Half Marathon 2025</title><link href="https://romain-thomas-shef.github.io/rt/blog/2025/morunner/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Morunner Half Marathon 2025"/><published>2025-11-16T12:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2025-11-16T12:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://romain-thomas-shef.github.io/rt/blog/2025/morunner</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://romain-thomas-shef.github.io/rt/blog/2025/morunner/"><![CDATA[<p>Last preparation race before the SaintLyon! This one is the MoRunner Half Marathon at Heaton Park in Manchester. It is made in support of Prostate cancer (hence the name). It is another looped race, with 4 loops of ~5k. There is a descent climb and the park is beautiful. Also it starts to be a bit cold! The race went fine and I finished it in 1h46 for a ranking of 35/213!</p> <swiper-container style="height: 500px;" keyboard="true" navigation="true" pagination="true" pagination-clickable="true" pagination-dynamic-bullets="true" rewind="true"> <swiper-slide style="display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; height: 100%;"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025morunner/map-480.webp 480w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025morunner/map-800.webp 800w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025morunner/map-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025morunner/map.png" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 m-0" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide style="display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center;"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025morunner/morunner1-480.webp 480w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025morunner/morunner1-800.webp 800w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025morunner/morunner1-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025morunner/morunner1.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 m-0" width="400px" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> </swiper-container>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="HM"/><category term="preparation"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Last race before the Saintelyon!]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Delamere forst trail Marathon 2025</title><link href="https://romain-thomas-shef.github.io/rt/blog/2025/delamere/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Delamere forst trail Marathon 2025"/><published>2025-11-02T12:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2025-11-02T12:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://romain-thomas-shef.github.io/rt/blog/2025/delamere</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://romain-thomas-shef.github.io/rt/blog/2025/delamere/"><![CDATA[<p>Here we go again after the halloween Marathon of last week! This time it is a trail Marathon in the Delamere forest. It is a bit far from my place so I am sleeping close to the race. I still managed to arrive 2min late for the race though! This is the first time I do a looped race. This one is four times 10.5k. Each loop start with a big climb and then wanders down to the forest. The colors were beautiful! The goal was not to push the speed but just to do the km so it was an easy pace. I did the 42k amnd 715m of climb in 4h26 which got me the 65 place in the ranking (out of 182).</p> <swiper-container style="height: 500px;" keyboard="true" navigation="true" pagination="true" pagination-clickable="true" pagination-dynamic-bullets="true" rewind="true"> <swiper-slide style="display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; height: 100%;"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025delamere/map-480.webp 480w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025delamere/map-800.webp 800w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025delamere/map-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025delamere/map.png" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 m-0" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide style="display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center;"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025delamere/delamere1-480.webp 480w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025delamere/delamere1-800.webp 800w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025delamere/delamere1-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025delamere/delamere1.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 m-0" width="600px" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide style="display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center;"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025delamere/delamere2-480.webp 480w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025delamere/delamere2-800.webp 800w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025delamere/delamere2-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025delamere/delamere2.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 m-0" width="600px" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> </swiper-container>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="Marathon"/><category term="preparation"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Let's increase the km!]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Worksop halloween Half Marathon 2025</title><link href="https://romain-thomas-shef.github.io/rt/blog/2025/HalloweenHM/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Worksop halloween Half Marathon 2025"/><published>2025-10-26T12:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2025-10-26T12:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://romain-thomas-shef.github.io/rt/blog/2025/HalloweenHM</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://romain-thomas-shef.github.io/rt/blog/2025/HalloweenHM/"><![CDATA[<p>Two weeks after Krakow I am doing another Half Marathon, this time in Worksop, one hour from Sheffield. I have never been here so it is a nice way to see a new place! This one is a bit more hilly compared to Krakow with 220m of ascent. It passes through Clumber park and the colors of autumn are really beautiful. Everything is on road. I finished it in 1h46 which is my second HM best time. Ranking was 355/1208.</p> <swiper-container style="height: 500px;" keyboard="true" navigation="true" pagination="true" pagination-clickable="true" pagination-dynamic-bullets="true" rewind="true"> <swiper-slide style="display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; height: 100%;"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025halloween/map-480.webp 480w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025halloween/map-800.webp 800w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025halloween/map-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025halloween/map.png" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 m-0" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide style="display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center;"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025halloween/halloween1-480.webp 480w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025halloween/halloween1-800.webp 800w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025halloween/halloween1-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025halloween/halloween1.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 m-0" width="600px" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide style="display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center;"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025halloween/halloween2-480.webp 480w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025halloween/halloween2-800.webp 800w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025halloween/halloween2-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025halloween/halloween2.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 m-0" width="600px" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> </swiper-container>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="HM"/><category term="preparation"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Halloween is here!]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Krakow Half Marathon 2025</title><link href="https://romain-thomas-shef.github.io/rt/blog/2025/krakowHM/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Krakow Half Marathon 2025"/><published>2025-10-12T12:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2025-10-12T12:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://romain-thomas-shef.github.io/rt/blog/2025/krakowHM</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://romain-thomas-shef.github.io/rt/blog/2025/krakowHM/"><![CDATA[<p>Let’s continue on the preparation of the Saintelyon with the Half Marathon of Krakow! The day was perfect for running, cloudy and not warm at all. It is a very nice race starting in the Tauron Arena and passing through the city center and along the river. Really enjoyed it! I finished it in 1:45: which is my half marathon PB! Ranking is 3898/14185 so that was quite a good race!</p> <swiper-container style="height: 500px;" keyboard="true" navigation="true" pagination="true" pagination-clickable="true" pagination-dynamic-bullets="true" rewind="true"> <swiper-slide style="display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; height: 100%;"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025krakowHM/map-480.webp 480w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025krakowHM/map-800.webp 800w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025krakowHM/map-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025krakowHM/map.png" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 m-0" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide style="display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center;"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025krakowHM/krk1-480.webp 480w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025krakowHM/krk1-800.webp 800w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025krakowHM/krk1-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025krakowHM/krk1.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 m-0" width="600px" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide style="display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center;"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025krakowHM/krk2-480.webp 480w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025krakowHM/krk2-800.webp 800w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025krakowHM/krk2-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025krakowHM/krk2.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 m-0" width="600px" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> </swiper-container>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="sample-posts"/><category term="HM"/><category term="preparation"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[First time running it]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Sheffield 10k 2025</title><link href="https://romain-thomas-shef.github.io/rt/blog/2025/Sheffield10k/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Sheffield 10k 2025"/><published>2025-09-28T12:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2025-09-28T12:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://romain-thomas-shef.github.io/rt/blog/2025/Sheffield10k</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://romain-thomas-shef.github.io/rt/blog/2025/Sheffield10k/"><![CDATA[<p>Back from holidays, this is the start of the saintlyon training at the end of November. This is the 2nd time I do it and it is a nice flatish 10k in the center of the city. It is a nice way to test a bit of speed! I finished the race in 48m22s which I am happy with!</p> <swiper-container style="height: 500px;" keyboard="true" navigation="true" pagination="true" pagination-clickable="true" pagination-dynamic-bullets="true" rewind="true"> <swiper-slide style="display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; height: 100%;"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025Shef10k/map-480.webp 480w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025Shef10k/map-800.webp 800w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025Shef10k/map-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025Shef10k/map.png" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 m-0" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide style="display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center;"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025Shef10k/shef10k-480.webp 480w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025Shef10k/shef10k-800.webp 800w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025Shef10k/shef10k-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025Shef10k/shef10k.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 m-0" width="400px" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> </swiper-container>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="sample-posts"/><category term="belowHM"/><category term="preparation"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Objective Saintelyon!]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Dig Deep 30 miles</title><link href="https://romain-thomas-shef.github.io/rt/blog/2025/digdeep30/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Dig Deep 30 miles"/><published>2025-08-30T12:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2025-08-30T12:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://romain-thomas-shef.github.io/rt/blog/2025/digdeep30</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://romain-thomas-shef.github.io/rt/blog/2025/digdeep30/"><![CDATA[<p>End of august, not much training during the summer but it is a local race so I wanted to do it (third time I enter the race, so I know it!). It litteraly starts 15minutes from my place. Coincidentally this is also the day after I moved from one appartment to a new one. Which was a bad idea… It was a beautiful day though, but after 20k and the win hill I started to have stomach problem so I prefered to drop out at an aid station around 30k.</p> <swiper-container style="height: 500px;" keyboard="true" navigation="true" pagination="true" pagination-clickable="true" pagination-dynamic-bullets="true" rewind="true"> <swiper-slide style="display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; height: 100%;"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025digdeep/digdeep25-480.webp 480w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025digdeep/digdeep25-800.webp 800w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025digdeep/digdeep25-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025digdeep/digdeep25.png" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 m-0" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> </swiper-container>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="ultra"/><category term="30miles"/><category term="fun"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[First DNF]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">The wall Ultra</title><link href="https://romain-thomas-shef.github.io/rt/blog/2025/thewall25/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="The wall Ultra"/><published>2025-06-14T12:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2025-06-14T12:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://romain-thomas-shef.github.io/rt/blog/2025/thewall25</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://romain-thomas-shef.github.io/rt/blog/2025/thewall25/"><![CDATA[<p>That’s the big one! It arrived! My first 100k! And also my Ultra #10. This one is called <a href="https://www.ratrace.com/events/the-wall/">“The Wall”</a>. It follows the Hadrian’s wall in the North of England. Hardian was a Roman Emperor. The race starts in Carlisle and finished in Newcastle; it goes from coast to coast. For this race I was not alone! Ola, my wife (&lt;3) is following the race with a car and will be there at aid stations, and my friend (and former colleague/Boss) Andrea, a German Astronomer leaving in Chile (where I used to work before) has decided to join me for this race. As I am quite scared of the 100k bar I am very happy to have someone running with me! The race started under a thunderstorm but the weather got better with the kms! It follows a really beautiful path with the most difficult being in the middle. We manage to finish the 111k in 15h33 (including pit stops). We ranked 230/1291.</p> <swiper-container style="height: 500px;" keyboard="true" navigation="true" pagination="true" pagination-clickable="true" pagination-dynamic-bullets="true" rewind="true"> <swiper-slide style="display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; height: 100%;"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025thewall/thewall5-480.webp 480w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025thewall/thewall5-800.webp 800w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025thewall/thewall5-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025thewall/thewall5.png" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 m-0" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide style="display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; height: 100%;"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025thewall/thewall1-480.webp 480w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025thewall/thewall1-800.webp 800w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025thewall/thewall1-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025thewall/thewall1.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 m-0" width="450px" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide style="display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; height: 100%"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025thewall/thewall2-480.webp 480w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025thewall/thewall2-800.webp 800w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025thewall/thewall2-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025thewall/thewall2.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 m-0" width="700px" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide style="display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; height: 100%"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025thewall/thewall3-480.webp 480w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025thewall/thewall3-800.webp 800w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025thewall/thewall3-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025thewall/thewall3.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 m-0" width="500px" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide style="display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; height: 100%"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025thewall/thewall4-480.webp 480w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025thewall/thewall4-800.webp 800w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025thewall/thewall4-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025thewall/thewall4.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 m-0" width="500px" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> </swiper-container>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="ultra"/><category term="100k"/><category term="objective"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[First 100k!]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Chester 50 miles</title><link href="https://romain-thomas-shef.github.io/rt/blog/2025/chester50/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Chester 50 miles"/><published>2025-03-15T12:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2025-03-15T12:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://romain-thomas-shef.github.io/rt/blog/2025/chester50</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://romain-thomas-shef.github.io/rt/blog/2025/chester50/"><![CDATA[<p>First ultra Marathon of the year. We are mid-March, weather is nice; cold but sunny. For this year I have chosen a race not to far from my place: Chester. This is part of the <a href="https://www.gbultras.com/">GBUltra</a> serie and it is a 50 miles, without much climbing. The start of the race was at 6am. Thes first part 30k is pretty boring and follows the canal while the last 50k is a bit more fun. In GB ultras you get different medal colors based on the ranking. The 200 first finish with a gold medal and I finished 182 our of 499. Iincluding aid station it took me 11h01 to complete the race. And I was on time in the evening to watch France with the 6 nations :)!</p> <swiper-container style="height: 500px;" keyboard="true" navigation="true" pagination="true" pagination-clickable="true" pagination-dynamic-bullets="true" rewind="true"> <swiper-slide style="display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; height: 100%;"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025chester50/chester6-480.webp 480w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025chester50/chester6-800.webp 800w,/rt/assets/img/runs/2025chester50/chester6-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/rt/assets/img/runs/2025chester50/chester6.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 m-0" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide style="display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; height: 100%;"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/r